One subtle point: the recover block assigns to the outer err. But the err from the opener loop is also in scope. No problem.

Also, the panic value could be a FrobError value (not a pointer) — the test panics with `panic(FrobError{tag, ...})`, so it's a value type. The type assertion `r.(FrobError)` works.

